endobj
342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (The data model contains three relationships, all following the One-to-Many \(1:*\) cardinality pattern with single-directional cross-filter direction, which is the recommended configuration for Star Schema models in Power BI.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Airline_Dim is connected to the Fact table through the airline field, with a One-to-Many cardinality and single filter direction flowing from the Dimension to the Fact table. This allows filtering flight records by carrier. Terminal_Dim is connected to the Fact table through the terminal field, with the same One-to-Many cardinality and single filter direction, enabling terminal-level analysis across all flight records. Destination_Dim is connected to the Fact table through the destination airport identifier, with One-to-Many cardinality and single filter direction. This relationship is essential for the International Flights % measure, which filters destinations to isolate domestic routes.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
